===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-cast aspersions.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[cast]] [[aspersion]]s}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To make [[damaging]] or [[spiteful]] [[remark]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Don't '''cast aspersions''' on me, or on my patriotism.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1911|author=Joseph Conrad|authorlink=Joseph Conrad|title=Under Western Eyes|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/files/2480/2480-h/2480-h.htm|passage=“You are '''casting aspersions''',” remonstrated Peter Ivanovitch, “which as far as you are concerned—” “No!” Razumov interrupted without heat. “Indeed, I don’t want to '''cast aspersions''', but it’s just as well to have no illusions.” Peter Ivanovitch gave him an inscrutable glance of his dark spectacles, accompanied by a faint smile. “The man who says that he has no illusions has at least that one,” he said, in a very friendly tone.}}

